{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "On Behalf Token Manager",
    "description": "**On Behalf Token Manager** manages delegate-member relationships and exposes\non-behalf access for delegates to act for members. It handles membership requests,\nmembership state (including revocation), and system insight.\n\n**What this service does**\n- **Manage delegate-member links**\n  - List a delegate's members, fetch an individual member, delete a member.\n  - **Revoke / restore** a member's access (`revokedAt` via `PUT /delegates/{id}/members/{memberId}`).\n  - Return an **on-behalf token** in the `member.token` object.\n- **Run the invitation workflow**\n  - Delegates **invite** prospective members; members **accept** or **cancel**.\n  - Delegates can **resend** or **delete** requests.\n- **System insight**\n  - `GET /info` provides config, health, and resource counters.\n- **User lifecycle (system)**\n  - System clients can delete a user by ID.\n\n**Conventions**\n- OAuth2 client-credentials for system/admin operations\n- Responses are JSON and typically wrapped in a top-level `data` property for consistency\n\n**Notes**\n- Examples are illustrative; field values are for demonstration only.\n- Use On Behalf Token Manager to centrally define on-behalf token trust, generate JWTs with the right scopes,\nand create user hierarchies with delegates and members.\n\n<p><a href='https://bitbucket.org/mimiktech/swagger-mobt/src'>Repository</a></p>\n",
    "contact": {
      "name": "mimik",
      "url": "https://developer.mimik.com/",
      "email": "support.sdk@mimik.com"
    },
